	(text "NIBBLE BOARD 03 - SEQUENCER: step counter, instruction and operand registers, flags, decoders and the diode control matrix"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "478bba7a-9d48-4600-a9cc-670e4ddfc229")
	)
	(text "Cell: 2N7000 + 47k pull-up (NMOS, see docs/gate-cell.md).  586 transistors, 352 resistors, 83 matrix diodes, 19 LEDs.\nFrom the bus header: M7..M0 (the program memory word), CF and ZF (from the ALU), CLK, RST.\nTo the bus header: II, PCE and the matrix columns SUB EO AI AO BI BO BA AB OI IO PCL FI HLT MAI MI MO ONE F0 F1 INP; BUS3#..BUS0# driven (open drain) with OPR3..0 while IO.\nTo board 09 (counter) over the LINK header: OPR7..0, PCR, RAI.  The program counter and the return register live there (D035).\nSteps S0..S4 are a one-hot ring of flip-flops: S0 loads IR/OPR (II), S1 counts (PCE), S2 loads the second word of a jump or call (OPI, PCE), S3 and S4 drive the matrix rows; DONE returns to S0.\ndocs/isa.md is the specification; sim/emu.py the reference the whole-machine simulation checks this board against."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f97803c2-5a1e-4e32-8d35-4f5361f6bffe")
	)
